        "source": "codechef",
        "standard_solution_code": "(limit, MOD) = (int(2 * 10 ** 6 + 10), int(10 ** 9) + 7)\n(factorial, invFactorial) = ([0] * limit, [0] * limit)\n\ndef calFactorial():\n\tlimit = int(2 * 10 ** 6 + 10)\n\t(factorial[0], factorial[1], invFactorial[0], invFactorial[1]) = (1, 1, 1, 1)\n\tfor i in range(2, limit):\n\t\tfactorial[i] = factorial[i - 1] * i % MOD\n\tfor i in range(2, limit):\n\t\tinvFactorial[i] = (MOD - MOD // i * invFactorial[MOD % i]) % MOD\n\tfor i in range(1, limit):\n\t\tinvFactorial[i] = invFactorial[i - 1] * invFactorial[i] % MOD\n\ndef nCr(N, R):\n\tif R > N:\n\t\treturn 0\n\tans = factorial[N] * invFactorial[R] % MOD * invFactorial[N - R]\n\tans %= MOD\n\treturn ans\n\ndef solve(N, K):\n\tans = 2 * nCr(N + K + 1, K + 2) - N\n\tans = (ans % MOD + MOD) % MOD\n\tprint(ans)\ncalFactorial()\nT = int(input())\nfor _ in range(T):\n\t(N, K) = map(int, input().split())\n\tsolve(N, K)"
